An opt-in `--detect-witness-matching-loops` option makes the matching-loop detection of automatically selected triggers follow the witnesses of nested existentials, so that a quantifier such as `forall q | q in s :: exists p :: p in s && q < p`, for example in a subset-type invariant, gets the matching-loop warning: each instance at `q` yields a fresh witness `p` with `p in s`, which matches the trigger `q in s` again (https://github.com/erniecohen/dafny/issues/202). Detection used to treat `p in s` as a harmless renaming of the trigger, since it differs only by one variable for another. A variable counts as a witness when its quantifier is skolemized whenever the enclosing one is instantiated: an existential in positive position, or a universal in negative position. With the option, a trigger that does not loop is preferred where one exists; otherwise the selected triggers are unchanged and the warning is reported. Disabled by default.
